<title>UK: SOCCER-BLACKBURN'S FLOWERS OUT FOR SEASON START.</title>
<headline>SOCCER-BLACKBURN'S FLOWERS OUT FOR SEASON START.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-07-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>New Blackburn manager Roy Hodgson will start the English premier league season without first choice goalkeeper Tim Flowers.</p>
<p>The England international was ruled out on Wednesday for the start of the season after undergoing surgery for a groin problem. John Filan will take his place.</p>
